"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"finishedAt\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"error\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"usage\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"sandboxKey\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"detachedSince\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"cancelRequested\""},{"type":"text","value":"\n| "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"driverEpoch\""},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-8","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"implementation-of-7","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Implementation of"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/RunStore.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunStore"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/RunStore.md#update","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"implements","text":"Implements","level":2},{"id":"constructors","text":"Constructors","level":2},{"id":"constructor","text":"Constructor","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"methods","text":"Methods","level":2},{"id":"createorresume","text":"createOrResume()","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"input","text":"input","level":5},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"implementation-of","text":"Implementation of","level":4},{"id":"findactiverun","text":"findActiveRun()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"threadid","text":"threadId","level":5},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"implementation-of-2","text":"Implementation of","level":4},{"id":"get","text":"get()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-3","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"runid","text":"runId","level":5},{"id":"returns-4","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"implementation-of-3","text":"Implementation of","level":4},{"id":"listbyparentrun","text":"listByParentRun()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-4","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"parentrunid","text":"parentRunId","level":5},{"id":"returns-5","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"implementation-of-4","text":"Implementation of","level":4},{"id":"listbythread","text":"listByThread()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-5","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"threadid-2","text":"threadId","level":5},{"id":"returns-6","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"implementation-of-5","text":"Implementation of","level":4},{"id":"listreclaimable","text":"listReclaimable()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-6","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"opts","text":"opts","level":5},{"id":"now","text":"now","level":6},{"id":"ttlms","text":"ttlMs","level":6},{"id":"returns-7","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"implementation-of-6","text":"Implementation of","level":4},{"id":"update","text":"update()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-7","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"runid-2","text":"runId","level":5},{"id":"patch","text":"patch","level":5},{"id":"returns-8","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"implementation-of-7","text":"Implementation of","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:370](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L370)\n\nIn-memory [RunStore](../interfaces/RunStore.md). Single process only.\n\n## Implements\n\n- [`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md)\n\n## Constructors\n\n### Constructor\n\n```ts\nnew InMemoryRunStore(): InMemoryRunStore;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`InMemoryRunStore`\n\n## Methods\n\n### createOrResume()\n\n```ts\ncreateOrResume(input): Promise<RunRecord>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:373](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L373)\n\nCreate a run record, or return the existing one unchanged if `runId` is\nalready present.\n\nINVARIANT (idempotency): an existing record is returned **unchanged** and\nthe passed `threadId`, `startedAt`, `status`, `parentRunId`,\n`subagentRunId`, and `name` are ignored. This is what makes resuming a\nrun safe. `status` defaults to `'running'` on first creation. The three\nlink fields are copied only on the first insert.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### input\n\n`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md), `\"threadId\"` \\| `\"runId\"` \\| `\"startedAt\"`\\> & `object`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`createOrResume`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#createorresume)\n\n***\n\n### findActiveRun()\n\n```ts\nfindActiveRun(threadId): Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:453](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L453)\n\nThe most recent `'running'` run for `threadId`, or `null` if none is active.\n\nREQUIRED. This resolves \"does this thread have a live run to attach to?\"\nfrom the STABLE thread id, which is the durable basis for reconnecting a\nclient (a reload, or the same thread opened on another device) — independent\nof the ephemeral run id, which a single turn may mint several of. When more\nthan one run is `'running'`, the one with the greatest `startedAt` wins.\n\nA backend that stubs this to `null` turns reconnect off silently, because\n`null` is also the correct answer for an idle thread. A backend with no run\nlifecycle at all should omit the whole `runs` store instead — capability\ntiers belong at the store level, not the method level.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`findActiveRun`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#findactiverun)\n\n***\n\n### get()\n\n```ts\nget(runId): Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:421](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L421)\n\nCurrent record, or null when unknown.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`get`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#get)\n\n***\n\n### listByParentRun()\n\n```ts\nlistByParentRun(parentRunId): Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:432](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L432)\n\nChild runs started by `parentRunId`, ascending by `startedAt`.\nOPTIONAL. `reconstructChat` uses this to put subagent cards back\non the parent assistant message. A store that omits it reloads the\ntext and not the cards.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### parentRunId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`listByParentRun`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#listbyparentrun)\n\n***\n\n### listByThread()\n\n```ts\nlistByThread(threadId): Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:425](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L425)\n\nEvery run in a conversation, ascending by `startedAt`. OPTIONAL.\n`reconstructChat` calls it to find the parent runs of children that a\ntool call started. Without it those cards stay absent on reload.\nConsumers feature-detect.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`listByThread`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#listbythread)\n\n***\n\n### listReclaimable()\n\n```ts\nlistReclaimable(opts): Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:439](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L439)\n\nRuns that may be reclaimed: ALL THREE of `status === 'running'`,\n`detachedSince` is set, and `detachedSince <= now - ttlMs`. The cutoff is\n**inclusive** — a run detached at exactly `now - ttlMs` IS reclaimable.\n\nOPTIONAL: only needed by a reaper. Consumers feature-detect.\n\n`detachedSince` is populated by `withSandbox`'s detach path (see\n[RunRecord.detachedSince](../interfaces/RunRecord.md#detachedsince)). The sweep over the candidates this\nsurfaces is `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `reapDetachedRuns`: it finalizes a run\nwhose agent already finished, expires one past its TTL, and reclaims the\nsandbox. That is a function, not a scheduler — the application invokes it\n(cron, queue, `alarm()`, `waitUntil`) — and a backend that omits this\nmethod cannot be reaped at all.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### opts\n\n###### now\n\n`number`\n\n###### ttlMs\n\n`number`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`listReclaimable`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#listreclaimable)\n\n***\n\n### update()\n\n```ts\nupdate(runId, patch): Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:400](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L400)\n\nPatch a record's mutable fields.\n\nINVARIANT: updating an unknown `runId` is a **no-op** — it must not throw\nand must not create a record.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n##### patch\n\n`Partial`\\<`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md), \n  \\| `\"status\"`\n  \\| `\"finishedAt\"`\n  \\| `\"error\"`\n  \\| `\"usage\"`\n  \\| `\"sandboxKey\"`\n  \\| `\"detachedSince\"`\n  \\| `\"cancelRequested\"`\n  \\| `\"driverEpoch\"`\\>\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`update`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#update)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: InMemoryRunStore\ntitle: InMemoryRunStore\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:370](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L370)\n\nIn-memory [RunStore](../interfaces/RunStore.md). Single process only.\n\n## Implements\n\n- [`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md)\n\n## Constructors\n\n### Constructor\n\n```ts\nnew InMemoryRunStore(): InMemoryRunStore;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`InMemoryRunStore`\n\n## Methods\n\n### createOrResume()\n\n```ts\ncreateOrResume(input): Promise<RunRecord>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:373](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L373)\n\nCreate a run record, or return the existing one unchanged if `runId` is\nalready present.\n\nINVARIANT (idempotency): an existing record is returned **unchanged** and\nthe passed `threadId`, `startedAt`, `status`, `parentRunId`,\n`subagentRunId`, and `name` are ignored. This is what makes resuming a\nrun safe. `status` defaults to `'running'` on first creation. The three\nlink fields are copied only on the first insert.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### input\n\n`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md), `\"threadId\"` \\| `\"runId\"` \\| `\"startedAt\"`\\> & `object`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`createOrResume`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#createorresume)\n\n***\n\n### findActiveRun()\n\n```ts\nfindActiveRun(threadId): Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:453](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L453)\n\nThe most recent `'running'` run for `threadId`, or `null` if none is active.\n\nREQUIRED. This resolves \"does this thread have a live run to attach to?\"\nfrom the STABLE thread id, which is the durable basis for reconnecting a\nclient (a reload, or the same thread opened on another device) — independent\nof the ephemeral run id, which a single turn may mint several of. When more\nthan one run is `'running'`, the one with the greatest `startedAt` wins.\n\nA backend that stubs this to `null` turns reconnect off silently, because\n`null` is also the correct answer for an idle thread. A backend with no run\nlifecycle at all should omit the whole `runs` store instead — capability\ntiers belong at the store level, not the method level.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`findActiveRun`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#findactiverun)\n\n***\n\n### get()\n\n```ts\nget(runId): Promise<RunRecord | null>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:421](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L421)\n\nCurrent record, or null when unknown.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md) \\| `null`\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`get`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#get)\n\n***\n\n### listByParentRun()\n\n```ts\nlistByParentRun(parentRunId): Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:432](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L432)\n\nChild runs started by `parentRunId`, ascending by `startedAt`.\nOPTIONAL. `reconstructChat` uses this to put subagent cards back\non the parent assistant message. A store that omits it reloads the\ntext and not the cards.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### parentRunId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`listByParentRun`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#listbyparentrun)\n\n***\n\n### listByThread()\n\n```ts\nlistByThread(threadId): Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:425](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L425)\n\nEvery run in a conversation, ascending by `startedAt`. OPTIONAL.\n`reconstructChat` calls it to find the parent runs of children that a\ntool call started. Without it those cards stay absent on reload.\nConsumers feature-detect.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### threadId\n\n`string`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`listByThread`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#listbythread)\n\n***\n\n### listReclaimable()\n\n```ts\nlistReclaimable(opts): Promise<RunRecord[]>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:439](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L439)\n\nRuns that may be reclaimed: ALL THREE of `status === 'running'`,\n`detachedSince` is set, and `detachedSince <= now - ttlMs`. The cutoff is\n**inclusive** — a run detached at exactly `now - ttlMs` IS reclaimable.\n\nOPTIONAL: only needed by a reaper. Consumers feature-detect.\n\n`detachedSince` is populated by `withSandbox`'s detach path (see\n[RunRecord.detachedSince](../interfaces/RunRecord.md#detachedsince)). The sweep over the candidates this\nsurfaces is `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`'s `reapDetachedRuns`: it finalizes a run\nwhose agent already finished, expires one past its TTL, and reclaims the\nsandbox. That is a function, not a scheduler — the application invokes it\n(cron, queue, `alarm()`, `waitUntil`) — and a backend that omits this\nmethod cannot be reaped at all.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### opts\n\n###### now\n\n`number`\n\n###### ttlMs\n\n`number`\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md)[]\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`listReclaimable`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#listreclaimable)\n\n***\n\n### update()\n\n```ts\nupdate(runId, patch): Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts:400](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/run-store.ts#L400)\n\nPatch a record's mutable fields.\n\nINVARIANT: updating an unknown `runId` is a **no-op** — it must not throw\nand must not create a record.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### runId\n\n`string`\n\n##### patch\n\n`Partial`\\<`Pick`\\<[`RunRecord`](../interfaces/RunRecord.md), \n  \\| `\"status\"`\n  \\| `\"finishedAt\"`\n  \\| `\"error\"`\n  \\| `\"usage\"`\n  \\| `\"sandboxKey\"`\n  \\| `\"detachedSince\"`\n  \\| `\"cancelRequested\"`\n  \\| `\"driverEpoch\"`\\>\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n\n#### Implementation of\n\n[`RunStore`](../interfaces/RunStore.md).[`update`](../interfaces/RunStore.md#update)\n"}
